{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHeckeRankOne","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHeckeRankOne","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.AdjoinRoot","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Quotient.Operations"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.commute_rankOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.commute_rankOne","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IwahoriHeckeRankOne.lean#L164-L170","doc":"**`H₂(q)` is commutative (sorry-free)** — a *corollary* of the identification,\nnot a prerequisite for it.  This is the statement the first version of this\nfile recorded as blocked. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.rankOneEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.rankOneEquiv","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IwahoriHeckeRankOne.lean#L150-L162","doc":"**The rank-1 identification (sorry-free).**  The rank-1 member of the uniform\nIwahori–Hecke family *is* `H₂(q) = K[X]/(X² - (q-1)X - q)`.  This is the first\nisomorphism in the corpus between the general-`n` family and a concrete rank\nobject. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.fromAdjoinRoot_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.fromAdjoinRoot_root","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IwahoriHeckeRankOne.lean#L146-L148","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.fromAdjoinRoot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.fromAdjoinRoot","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IwahoriHeckeRankOne.lean#L138-L144","doc":"The inverse comparison map, via `Ideal.Quotient.liftₐ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.evalSigma_heckePoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.evalSigma_heckePoly","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IwahoriHeckeRankOne.lean#L130-L136","doc":"**The Hecke quadratic dies in `H` (sorry-free).**  This is what lets the\nevaluation descend through the quotient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.evalSigma_C","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.evalSigma_C","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IwahoriHeckeRankOne.lean#L126-L128","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.evalSigma_X","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.evalSigma_X","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IwahoriHeckeRankOne.lean#L123-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.evalSigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.evalSigma","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IwahoriHeckeRankOne.lean#L116-L121","doc":"Evaluation `K[X] →ₐ[K] H` at the Hecke generator.  Uses the\n**noncommutative-target** eval: the only hypothesis is that scalars commute\nwith `σ₀`, which `Algebra.commutes` supplies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.toAdjoinRoot_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.toAdjoinRoot_σ","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IwahoriHeckeRankOne.lean#L104-L109","doc":"**The comparison map is non-degenerate (sorry-free):** it carries the Hecke\ngenerator `σ₀` to the adjoined root.  Without this the map above would be\ncompatible with being constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.toAdjoinRoot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.toAdjoinRoot","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IwahoriHeckeRankOne.lean#L91-L102","doc":"**The rank-1 comparison map (sorry-free).**  `H₂(q) = IwahoriHecke K q 1`\nmaps to `K[X]/(X² - (q-1)X - q)`.  The braid and commutation constructors are\ndischarged by `omega`: both are uninhabited at `n = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.root_quad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.root_quad","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IwahoriHeckeRankOne.lean#L78-L89","doc":"**The `AdjoinRoot` generator satisfies the Hecke quadratic (sorry-free).**\nStated in the `smul` form used by `HeckeRel.quadratic`, so it plugs directly\ninto the `RingQuot` lift below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.heckePoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.heckePoly","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IwahoriHeckeRankOne.lean#L75-L76","doc":"The Hecke quadratic `X² - (q-1)X - q` as a polynomial over `K`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}